-- title:
--   Unique infinitesimal lifting of 𝒪-algebra maps out of 𝒪^{nr}
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$. Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, let $\pi \in \mathcal O$ be irreducible, assume $\mathcal O$ is adically complete for the ideal $(\pi)$, that the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements, and that $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$ (absolute unramifiedness). Let $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a characteristic-zero commutative domain which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, such that every $x \in \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies $f(x) \equiv 0 \pmod{\pi}$ for some monic $f \in \mathcal O[X]$, and such that every monic polynomial of positive degree over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo $\pi$. Let $B$ and $B_0$ be commutative $\mathcal O$-algebras in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, and let $p : B \to B_0$ be a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map whose kernel is square-zero, in the form that $s t = 0$ whenever $p(s) = p(t) = 0$. Then for every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi_0 : \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B_0$ there is a unique $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ with $\psi$ followed by $p$ equal to $\psi_0$.
--
--   This is the formal étaleness of the unramified coefficient ring $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ over its absolutely unramified base $\mathcal O$, tested on $\pi$-nilpotent algebras: unique lifting of $\mathcal O$-algebra maps along square-zero surjections. It supplies the rigidity used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld lifting lemmas and, through them, in the construction of fine families for the quaternionic moduli problem; the proof passes through the identification of $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ with a Witt vector ring over its algebraically closed residue field, where the corresponding Witt-vector lifting statement is available.
